        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(signal): include quoted reply context for agents",
        "body": "Closes #98287\nRelated: #98234 (non-duplicate reply-session initialization conflict/drop issue)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where Signal users sending quoted replies could have the quoted target extracted into `ReplyToBody` metadata while the agent-facing `BodyForAgent` remained only the new ambiguous message, such as `Did this get done?`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSignal inbound handling now renders visible quoted-reply context directly into `BodyForAgent` as a clear blockquote while preserving clean `RawBody`, `CommandBody`, and `BodyForCommands` for command parsing and hooks. The shared inbound metadata renderer skips only the duplicate one-hop reply-target block when the Signal-generated wrapper exactly matches the expected quoted body and sender; richer `ReplyChain` context and ordinary user-authored blockquotes still render normally.\n\n## User Impact\n\nSignal quoted replies now carry the referenced message into agent-facing input, so agents can answer ambiguous followups using the intended quoted target. Plain non-quoted Signal messages remain unchanged, and quoted context is not duplicated in the model prompt when Signal has already inlined the generated quote block.\n\n## Evidence\n\nDuplicate search before filing found no open narrow issue/PR for `Signal quoted reply BodyForAgent` / `agent-facing body`; the closest existing items were closed #68665 and related-but-different #84364, plus broad open quote-reply PRs that do not provide this narrow BodyForAgent fix.\n\nValidation run locally:\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.inbound-context.test.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.mention-gating.test.ts extensions/signal/src/inbound-context.contract.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/inbound-meta.test.ts`\n- `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.extensions.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/extensions.tsbuildinfo && node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo`\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/signal/src` (29 files, 375 tests)\n- `git diff --check`\n- Exact-head regression coverage now canonicalizes blank lines in multi-paragraph quoted text (`>` with no trailing space) and proves the duplicate metadata block stays suppressed.\n- Debounced Signal batches now render reply context per entry before joining the batch, with quoted-first/plain-last and plain-first/quoted-last regressions and an internal exact-once marker that preserves the last structured reply metadata without duplicating it in the prompt.\n- Fresh GitHub CI is running after the only preceding failure—two formatter-only line wraps in the Signal handler—was fixed on exact head `8087d6f852d51bf20dd0bca1d13c900219d6e3ed`, which includes the shared upstream cutoff `262baedcf7fa3d66dc35cce7d0253e0a31f0cc0e`.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.ts extensions/signal/src/monitor/event-handler.inbound-context.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/inbound-meta.ts src/auto-reply/reply/inbound-meta.test.ts`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode local --prompt 'Review the final Signal quoted-reply BodyForAgent change after exact generated-prefix duplicate checks that include expected sender and boundary. Confirm no accepted duplicate-context, equal-body, spoofed marker/altered wrapper, ReplyChain, or command/raw body regressions remain.'` clean with no accepted/actionable findings.\n\nCaveat: no live Signal device roundtrip was run in this isolated checkout. The proof is source-level focused tests, the full Signal plugin Vitest directory, TypeScript checks, format/whitespace checks, and autoreview.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; no agent transcript is included because this task involved private Signal context and the local transcript prompt flow was unavailable in this run mode.\n",
